<title>UK: Dixons down after chairman sells shares.</title>
<headline>Dixons down after chairman sells shares.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Dixons Group Plc fell on Monday as investor confidence wavered after the group's chairman, Sir Stanley Kalms, sold off over one million shares on Friday, market makers said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 16p at 501 by 0838 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;Stanley Kalms sold some shares and people are a bit nervous,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>On Friday, January 31, Kalms excerised a share option and sold some 102,000 ordinary shares at 520p each. Simultaneously, a total of 1.0 million shares owned beneficially by Kalms and his wife were sold at 520p per share.</p>
<p>-- Paul Carrel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
